			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3845977">
									

<p>Excellent news. Keter feels wrong somehow, and Archon fills an interesting niche in the box metaphor:</p>
<ul>
<li>If you lock it in a box, leave it alone, and nothing bad will happen, then it's probably Safe.</li>
<li>If you lock it in a box, leave it alone, and you're not entirely sure what will happen, then it's probably Euclid.</li>
<li>If you lock it in a box, leave it alone, and it easily escapes, then it's probably Keter.</li>
<li>If it is the box, then it's probably Thaumiel.</li>
<li>If locking it in a box is the cause of bad things happening, it's probably Archon.</li>
</ul>

