<p>This is really good! There's another article that uses a similar esoteric class, though: <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-3240">http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-3240</a> is Hiemal-class, described by Niles as &quot;putting it in a box makes other bad shit start happening&quot;. I know Pickman used Archon-class for his 001 proposal, but this might fit better as Hiemal. Up to you, and regardless, you get a +1.</p>
<p>Other thoughts:</p>
<p>- My immediate reaction was &quot;hey, it's the Dark Hour from Persona 3 as an SCP&quot;. I'm not sure if that's what you intended or not, but I like it.<br />
- Pure curiosity, but is there any historical basis for a month called Liberary? Like, has it ever been on any calendar?<br />
- Is there any significance to the interviewer's name being Christchurch? Considering the religious implications of the SCP, it seems almost too apropos.</p>

							</div>

								
					
